"""TouchDesigner MCP bootstrap — run from a Text or Execute DAT on the host thread."""
import datetime
import json
import os
import sys

_WHEEL = {adapter_path}
_ADAPTER_PATH = _WHEEL
_ERROR_LOG = os.environ.get(
    "DCC_MCP_TOUCHDESIGNER_BOOTSTRAP_ERROR_LOG",
    os.path.join(os.path.expanduser("~"), ".dcc-mcp", "logs", "touchdesigner-bootstrap.jsonl"),
)


def _record_bootstrap(payload):
    payload["timestamp"] = datetime.datetime.now(datetime.timezone.utc).isoformat()
    os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(_ERROR_LOG), exist_ok=True)
    with open(_ERROR_LOG, "a", encoding="utf-8") as stream:
        stream.write(json.dumps(payload, sort_keys=True) + "\n")
        stream.flush()
        os.fsync(stream.fileno())


try:
    if not os.path.exists(_ADAPTER_PATH):
        raise RuntimeError("TouchDesigner adapter path not found: %s" % _ADAPTER_PATH)
    if _WHEEL not in sys.path:
        sys.path.insert(0, _WHEEL)
    import dcc_mcp_touchdesigner

    server = dcc_mcp_touchdesigner.start_server()
except BaseException as exc:
    try:
        _record_bootstrap(
            {
                "stage": "initialize",
                "success": False,
                "exception_type": type(exc).__name__,
                "reason": str(exc),
            }
        )
    except OSError:
        pass
    raise
else:
    try:
        _record_bootstrap({"stage": "initialize", "success": True})
    except OSError:
        pass
    print("[dcc-mcp-touchdesigner] MCP server listening at %s" % server.mcp_url)
